    "title": "Is 'The Bachelorette' on tonight? What will replace 'The Bachelorette'",
    "text": "March 22, 2026, 2:00 p.m. MTABC's \"The Bachelorette\" won't be premiering tonight as originally planned.Season 22 was officially canceled on Thursday, March 19, after a video of an altercation between lead Taylor Frankie Paul and ex Dakota Mortensen was released on Thursday, March 19, by TMZ.News also broke on March 17 that Paul and Mortensen were being investigated in connection with a \"blowup\" while filming \"The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives\" Season 5. TMZ broke the news that the investigation caused production to stop.Here's when \"The Bachelorette\" was supposed to premiere and what will be airing in its place.When was 'The Bachelorette' supposed to air?\"The Bachelorette\" Season 22 was going to premiere on Sunday, March 22.Is 'The Bachelorette' going to air?No. \"The Bachelorette\" 2026 was canceled on Thursday, March 19.Is 'The Bachelorette' on tonight?\"The Bachelorette\" will not be airing tonight, March 22.Has ABC canceled 'The Bachelorette'?Yes, ABC canceled this season of \"The Bachelorette.\"\"In light of the newly released video just surfaced today, we have made the decision to not move forward with the new season of 'The Bachelorette' at this time, and our focus is on supporting the family,\" a Disney Entertainment Television spokesperson told USA TODAY Thursday, March 19.Why was 'The Bachelorette' canceled?Taylor Frankie Paul's season of \"The Bachelorette\" was canceled after TMZ released an old 2023 video showing an altercation between Paul and Mortensen.In the video, released on March 19, Paul appears to be hitting and throwing metal chairs at Mortensen. The two seem to be arguing.\"Your daughter is right here,\" Mortensen says before two more chairs are thrown by Paul.A child is then heard crying in the background as Paul blames Mortensen.\"Stop throwing stuff and help your daughter,\" Mortensen says. \"Help your daughter. Stop screaming at me. God. Stop, Taylor.\"More shuffling and fighting is heard in the background, but it is unclear what is happening as it is not shown on camera.What will replace 'The Bachelorette'?Instead of Season 22, Episode 1 of \"The Bachelorette,\" a rerun of \"American Idol\" will be airing on Sunday, March 22, at 7 p.m. Arizona time and 8 p.m. ET/PT.Who won 'The Bachelorette' 2026?Before getting canceled, Reality Steve posted spoilers on Tuesday, March 17, about Taylor Frankie Paul's season.Hometown dates included Shane Parton from Atlanta, Lew Evans from Salt Lake City, Doug Mason from San Diego and Casey Hux from Nashville. Overnight dates were with Parton, Evans and Mason, with Evans being eliminated ahead of the final two.Her finale was filmed in St. Lucia, according to Reality Steve and Paul got engaged to 28-year-old Mason.Did Taylor Frankie Paul get engaged on 'The Bachelorette'?Paul ended the season engaged to Mason, but the two ended their relationship following the conclusion of filming. Reality Steve said this is due to Paul's ex, Mortensen.According to Reality Steve, Paul never got over her ex, Mortensen. It was revealed to the public in Season 4, Episode 10 of \"The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives\" that Paul had slept with Mortensen the night before leaving for filming of \"The Bachelorette.\"Mason apparently flew to Utah a month after the engagement, around January, according to Reality Steve, and Paul ended things.Where to watch 'The Bachelorette'?Although the new season won't be premiering, you can catch up on old seasons of \"The Bachelorette\" on Hulu.A subscription to Hulu costs $11.99 a month (or $119.99/year) for the ad-supported plan. Students can get Hulu with ads for $1.99 a month, and Hulu Premium costs $18.99 a month.Do you have a tip or a question you need answered? Reach the reporter at dina.kaur@arizonarepublic.com. Follow @dina_kaur on X, formerly known as Twitter, and on Instagram @dina_kaur.Support local journalism. Subscribe to azcentral.com today.",
